      "closure_rationale": "One trusted field registry derives native declarations, names/offsets/sizes, typed access, descriptors, validation, presence-aware equality, explicit tagged wire and ordered visitors. Actual codec.records ar_encode/ar_decode version2 handles the optional signed field. Retained six-octet registry producer and MOD11/12 controls are actually executed; no native padding is serialized. Inspected N1570 layout, substitution, stringification, token-concatenation and offsetof passages distinguish C11 draft rules from unavailable published C17/C23. Actual Rust2021 macro_rules plus derived PartialEq includes a new field, with no C ABI/hygiene or arbitrary-reflection equivalence. Complete-input hash words and observed linker symbol significance are separate build enforcement, not ISO language introspection or authentication. Six profiles pass4anchors and8compiled ordinary semantic controls;4compiling stubs reject. Every profile matches9811 independent encode/decode/visitor cases, including1390accepted and40callback-stop outcomes. Seven10000-encode samples, real object/stack/helper costs and clean/unchanged build observations retain exact contracts. GCC/Clang consistently packed native layouts change offsets while preserving independently specified wire bytes. Required quality field transfer adds tag4,width2,since3,range0..15 and exercises generated decode/equality/validation/visitor plus version2-to3 migration and refusal to downgrade a present field. An old handwritten equality still compiles and demonstrably misses quality. Actual stale full-input check, four-word compile assertion and old-object link guards reject; regenerated consumers execute. Generated compiler header bytes and recipe are explicitly verified and archived rather than bypassing dependency closure. Delayed independent learner evidence remains unassessed. Bounded author support only."
    },
